From 9e57ee4ab63e6b77642c9338d3f94ebe72e029d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josh Boyd <boydjd@jbip.net>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:33:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01/17] hw/riscv: add Espressif ESP32-S31 machine with
 CLIC-mode harts

Adds an "esp32s31" machine (HP core 0) and "esp32s31" CPU model:
- target/riscv: Espressif-style CLIC operating in CLIC mode (traps with
  xcause.exccode = input id, xtvec[5:0] forced, xcause.xpp/xpie aliases,
  xpil and interrupt levels, xret level restore for interrupt-type
  xcause only, S-mode sie/sip trap), wfi wakeup
- vendor PMA CSRs
- CLIC (M and S banks), interrupt matrix, SYSTIMER, UART0, LP AON
  reset, flash XIP window, PSRAM, HP/LP SRAM, mask ROM stubs
- emulates the U-Boot SPL: boots a raw 16MiB flash image by loading the
  U-Boot FIT (OpenSBI fw_dynamic + U-Boot + dtb)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0158d423kzUx8WWBMMEZ95NX
